---
import DownloadButtons from "../download/DownloadButtons.astro";
import Page from "../site/Page.astro";
import { RELEASES } from "../site/links.ts";
---

<Page title="Get started — Katari" description="Which Katari to download, how it updates, and how to bring your library over.">
  <main>
    <h1>Get started</h1>
    <p class="lead">Answers to what comes up between downloading Katari and reading in it.</p>

    <details id="which-file" open>
      <summary>Which file should I download?</summary>
      <div class="answer">
        <p>
          Katari runs on phones and tablets with Android 10 or newer. Most people want <strong>Katari</strong>. The
          same app without Google services is <strong>Katari FOSS</strong>, which never sends crash logs or usage data.
        </p>
        <DownloadButtons explained={false} />
        <p>
          Both come as smaller builds for one kind of processor too: arm64-v8a for most phones of recent years, and
          armeabi-v7a for older ones. They are on the <a href={`${RELEASES}/latest`}>release page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Does Katari update itself?</summary>
      <div class="answer">
        <p>
          Yes, both builds do. When a new version is out, Katari offers to download and install it. Android asks once
          for permission to let Katari install apps.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Can I bring my library over from Mihon?</summary>
      <div class="answer">
        <p>
          Yes. In Mihon, create a backup containing everything you want to keep, then choose it when Katari's setup
          offers <em>Move from Mihon</em>. Include private settings to bring source preferences and sign-ins along.
        </p>
        <p>
          To keep your downloads, select the storage folder Mihon used. Extensions installed privately in Mihon need to
          be installed again.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Where does the content come from?</summary>
      <div class="answer">
        <p>
          Katari comes with no content and has no affiliation with any provider. Sources are extensions you choose: add
          an extension store under Browse › Extensions, then install the extensions you want from it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>What does Katari send, and can I turn it off?</summary>
      <div class="answer">
        <p>
          Katari can send anonymized crash logs and usage data. Its setup shows both as switches, and you can change
          them any time in Settings › Security and privacy. Katari FOSS sends neither.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </main>
</Page>

<script>
  // A link to a question, such as the header's Download, has to show its answer even when the visitor closed it.
  const openQuestion = (hash: string) => {
    const target = hash.length > 1 ? document.getElementById(decodeURIComponent(hash.slice(1))) : null;
    const question = target?.closest("details");
    if (question) question.open = true;
  };
  openQuestion(location.hash);
  addEventListener("hashchange", () => openQuestion(location.hash));
  // Following a link to the anchor already in the address changes no hash, so the click itself has to open it.
  document.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
    const link = (event.target as Element).closest("a");
    if (link && link.pathname === location.pathname && link.hash) openQuestion(link.hash);
  });
</script>

<style>
  main {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem var(--gutter) 0;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 3.6rem);
  }

  .lead {
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--indigo-light);
  }

  summary {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.2rem 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  summary::after {
    content: "+";
    color: var(--clay);
    font-family: var(--sans);
  }

  details[open] summary::after {
    content: "−";
  }

  .answer {
    padding: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .answer p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .answer strong,
  .answer em {
    color: var(--cream);
  }

  .answer :global(.download) {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
</style>
